# Dependency Hygiene

## Minimal dependencies
Only add a package if it provides significant value that would take substantial effort to build. Prefer the platform (native browser APIs, Node built-ins) over libraries when reasonable.

## No version pinning to old releases
When adding a dependency, always install the latest stable version. Never copy a version number from memory or examples — use `npm install <package>` to get the current release.

## Security
If `npm audit` reports vulnerabilities, address them before shipping. Do not ignore audit warnings.

## Monthly check (manual, not enforced by AI)
Once a month, run:
```bash
npm outdated
npm audit
```
Update packages that have minor/patch releases. For major version bumps, review the changelog before updating.

## When updating dependencies:
- Update one package at a time
- Run tests after each update
- Commit each update separately
- Never batch multiple major version bumps into one commit
